, "tokens_before": 37105, "tokens_after": 37105, "ok": true, "error": ""}, {"step_id": "step_16", "tool": "window_event_count", "args": {"windows": [[27001, 28000], [28001, 29000], [29001, 30000], [30001, 31000], [31001, 32000]], "nodes": [1885, 1572, 826, 1460]}, "result_digest": "2b0d4fba4de1faab", "result_summary": "{\"counts\": [{\"n_events\": 1, \"window\": [27001, 28000]}, {\"n_events\": 0, \"window\": [28001, 29000]}, {\"n_events\": 0, \"window\": [29001, 30000]}, {\"n_events\": 2, \"window\": [30001, 31000]}, {\"n_events\": 2, \"window\": [31001, 32000]}]}", "latency_ms": 5, "tokens_before": 37105, "tokens_after": 37105, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_9cf28e7b", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [1885, 1460], "window": [3683, 42083], "confidence": 0.89, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "1885's entire out-cone is the chain 1885->1572->826, and 826's own 2-hop closure is a small 14-node cluster that excludes 1460 and both of 1460's only in-neighbours (765, 1045). Backward expansion from 1460 yields a disjoint node set. Hence no directed path exists even with time ignored, so no time-respecting cascade with \u0394t<=600 can exist. High overall event volume and the presence of hubs (1132, 1682) elsewhere in the graph do not bridge these two components; 1885 and 1460 are themselves low-degree with non-overlapping sparse activity."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Forward reachability from 1885 (directed, out-edges):**\n- 1885 has only one out-partner: 1572 (step_05)\n- 1572 \u2192 826 only (step_08)\n- 826 \u2192 {676, 1485, 1580} (step_10)\n- The 2-hop closure around 826 (= 4 hops from 1885) is a small closed cluster of 14 nodes: {197, 511, 676, 733, 826, 908, 1232, 1439, 1485, 1572, 1693, 1702, 1885, 1986} (step_15) \u2014 it does **not** contain 1460, nor either of 1460's only in-neighbours (765, 1045; step_04).\n\n**Backward from 1460:** only 765 and 1045 ever contact 1460 in the window (step_04); their in-neighbours are {149, 1081, 1132, 1210, 1382} and {981, 1682, 1992} (steps 06, 07) \u2014 disjoint from the 1885 forward cone.\n\nSo there is no directed path from 1885 to 1460 at all, even **ignoring** time; the \u0394t \u2264 600 constraint is moot.\n\n**Confounder controls:** the window is busy (7,236 events, 1,950 active nodes, step_01), and the path passes through/near hubs (1132 with 162 events, 1682 with 48 events, step_09) \u2014 high volume and hub popularity could suggest connectivity, but 1885 and 1460 are themselves near-isolated (4 and 3 events, step_02). Their activity is also temporally scattered: 1885's events fall in [17k\u201337k] and 1572's only in [27k\u201332k] (steps 12, 13), while 1460's three events are spread across 12k\u201332k (step_14), with only sparse, non-contiguous bursts in the one overlapping sub-region (step_16).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_9cf28e7b\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1885, 1460],\n  \"window\": [3683, 42083],\n  \"confidence\": 0.89,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1885's entire out-cone is the chain 1885->1572->826, and 826's own 2-hop closure is a small 14-node cluster that excludes 1460 and both of 1460's only in-neighbours (765, 1045). Backward expansion from 1460 yields a disjoint node set. Hence no directed path exists even with time ignored, so no time-respecting cascade with \u0394t<=600 can exist. High overall event volume and the presence of hubs (1132, 1682) elsewhere in the graph do not bridge these two components; 1885 and 1460 are themselves low-degree with non-overlapping sparse activity.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 45630, "total_output_tokens": 5116, "total_tokens": 50746, "total_latency_ms": 77558, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}